'---- General Comments on the Entry --------'
' 3 Menus 'SO', 'PL', 'QT', 'QS' all similar, except
'   in 'PL' only one record per Customer, Design, Size, Suffix combination allowed.
'   SO is used for entering the Sales Orders
'   QT is used for entering the Quotations
'   PL is the Party-Design Combination Master
'
' X-OrdMst, A-OrdDsg, B-OrdRm, C-OrdLab
'
' TabPage, TabSumm, 3 Tabs
'   1. Design Rm & Lab Summmary
'      This tab is used for displaying the Rm & Lab totals for the current row of GrdOrdDsg
'      The Rm Details can be seen Ctg/SCtg/RmCd wise by selecting the appropriate
'      group option in the Rm Group By Option
'      The Lab Details can be seen Lab MainCd/SubCd wise depending on the group option
'      selected in the 'Lab Group By' Option
'   2. Order Design Summary
'      This tab is used for displaying the Design totals for the entire voucher
'      The Details can be seen OrdCTg/DsgCd/Sr wise by selecting the appropriate
'      group option in the Dsg Group By Option
'   3. Order Rm & Lab Summary
'      This tab is used for displaying the Rm & Lab totals for the entire voucher
'      The Rm Details can be seen Ctg/SCtg/RmCd wise by selecting the appropriate
'      group option in the Rm Group By Option
'      The Lab Details can be seen Lab MainCd/SubCd wise by selecting the appropriate
'      group option in the Lab Group By Option
' CmdOrdCpy to copy from another order  (Copy of the entire Order)
'   wOmTc, wOmYy, wOmChr, wOmNo, wCustFr, wCpyRt, CmdOrdCpyGo are the fields on the FraOrdCpy Frame
'   This option is enabled only if there are no Design records.
' CmdOrdDet to show the Order Details
'   This includes all the fields of the OrdMst Table which could not fit into
'   the NonKeyAll frame
' CmdDsgDet to show the Design Details
'   This includes all the fields of the OrdDsg Table which could not fit into
'   the grid GrdOrdDsg for display purposes.
' CmdDsgCpy to copy from Party-Dsg Combination Master of the given Cust or from ZSELF or DsgMst
'   wDsgDmCd, wDsgSfx, wDsgSz, wDsgSrNo, wDsgCpyRt, wDsgSource, wDsgSrcVch, CmdDsgCpyGo
' CmdOrdAmd to show the Order Amendment frame
'   GrdOrdAmd records of OrdAmd table
' CmdSumm to show the Summary frame FraSumm (the Summary frame contains the TabPage TabSumm and the frame for each tab FraTabSumm)
'   GrdDsgRmSumm, GrdDsgLabSumm, wDsgRmGrp, wDsgRmTotQty, wDsgRmTotWt, wDsgRmTotVal,
'     wDsgLabGrp, wDsgLabTotVal are the controls in the frame FraTabSumm(0)
'   GrdOrdDsgSumm, wOrdDsgGrp, wOrdDsgTotQty, wOrdDsgTotVal are the controls in the frame FraTabSumm(1)
'   GrdOrdRmSumm, GrdOrdLabSumm, wOrdRmGrp, wOrdLabGrp, wOrdRmTotQty, wOrdRmTotWt, wOrdRmTotVal, wOrdLabTotVal
'     are the controls in the frame FraTabSumm(2)
'   Private Subs : DsgRmSumm, DsgLabSumm
' CmdSC to show the scope frame. This option is available only in the 'PDC' menu option.
'   This CommandButton is enabled when the cursor is in the Key Frame. This is useful in PDC
'   when the user wants to see the records of only a particular design category(s) or
'   of a range of Designs
'   wSCDmCtgFr, wSCDmCtgTo, wSCDmCdFr, wSCDmCdTo are the controls on the FraSC frame
'
' Image controls  PicHsk for the pencil Sketch, Pic3d for the 3-D image.
'   These image controls are placed on the frames FraPicHsk & FraPic3D respectively
' Enlarged state of the pictures can be obtained by double clicking on the pictures
' The pictures can be brought back to the original size by again double clicking the pictures
'--------------------

